{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310769,"nonce":"mrWbRPH+17/w4ALoV5+1S3zz9Aw=","title":"TWO landed things (2026-07-13). (1) COMPILER CAPABILITY: extern classes can now have CONCRETE body-bearing methods (non-@:native, with a { ...","message":"An `extern class` (e.g. `Sys`) can now declare a NORMAL method WITH a body\n(no `@:native`) — it compiles to MIR and dispatches as a direct call. Bodyless\n`@:native` methods in the same class are unaffected. `inline` does NOT work as a\nsubstitute (extern dispatch overrode it); the real fix was two body-gated spots:\n- `compilation.rs` `is_extern_only`: a file whose decls are all extern classes\n  was skipped before MIR, dropping any concrete body. Now `has_concrete_method`\n  (any class/abstract method with non-empty `body`) keeps the file in MIR\n  lowering. hir_to_mir's per-method guards (2749/2895) still skip the bodyless\n  `@:native` methods, so NO wrong-signature stubs.\n- `compilation.rs` `register_extern_methods_from_typed_file`: skip methods with\n  a body. Registering a body-bearing method as a bare-name extern mapping made\n  the call resolve to a nonexistent runtime symbol (\"can't resolve symbol X\").\nDEBUG TECHNIQUE that pinned it: `rayzor compile \u003cf\u003e --stage {ast,tast,hir,mir}`\n+ grep the fn's `(N blocks)` — 0 blocks past HIR = body dropped. Non-extern\ncontrol class (4 blocks) vs extern (0 blocks) isolated the cause. `--no-cache`\nREQUIRED (stdlib Sys.hx is BLADE-cached).\n\n`Sys.getEnvOr(name, alias)` (compiler/haxe-std/Sys.hx) is the first consumer:\nreturns getEnv(name) ?? getEnv(alias) ?? null.\n\n- **RZT_*** = rayzor-tensors plugin (shared kernel/pool): USE_SDOT, NEON_SILU,\n  KERNEL_TIMING, LEGACY_{KERNEL,POOL}, WORKERS, QOS, NO_{CALLER_BAND,PARK},\n  STATIC_BANDS, POOL[_DISABLE/_STATS/_MAX_*], TENSOR_{POOL_POISON,ALLOC_HISTOGRAM*},\n  SILU_MUL_PAR_THRESHOLD, PREFILL_MORSELS. Read via `rayzor_tensors::env_var(\n  primary, legacy)` (Result-typed helper in rayzor-tensors/src/lib.rs).\n- **NUE_*** = nue inference: MATMUL, FLASH*, FUSED_MATMUL, MATMUL_WORKERS,\n  POOL_{PROFILE,SPINS,RELAX}, KV_Q8, REQUANT_{LM_HEAD,Q6K}, PREFILL_LAST_LOGITS,\n  PROFILE_{POOL,DECODE*,LOAD}, LLAMA_*, DUMP_*, SPEC_DECODE, SERVER_*,\n  FREE_GGUF_BYTES. Read via `Sys.getEnvOr(\"NUE_X\", \"RAYZOR_...\")`.\n- **RAYZOR_*** STAYS = CORE only (NO_PRELOAD_MMAP, NO_MLOCK_MMAP, STDOUT_FLUSH_MS,\n  PERF_AFFINITY, HEAP_CHECK, DUMP_FN_PTRS, CPU_PROFILE*, ...). Core reads ZERO\n  inference env now (the plugin moves drained it). The pool reads NUE_MATMUL (the\n  caller's gate) — layering wart pending a caller-hint param.\n- Legacy `RAYZOR_HAXE_*` / `RAYZOR_*` names ALL still work (alias arg). Scripts\n  (run_bundle.sh, bench_server.sh) use canonical names; 2 dead vars\n  (HAXE_FLASH_BATCH_MAX, LLAMA_STREAM_FLUSH_MS) read nowhere — left as-is.\n- Verified behaviorally: `[kv-cache] Q8_0 mode enabled` fires for BOTH\n  NUE_KV_Q8=1 and RAYZOR_KV_Q8=1, absent when unset. Harness 166/166.\n\nRelated: [[project_three_layer_architecture]], [[perf_haxe_kernel_pool_cooperation_blocker]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `feature_extern_method_bodies_and_env_split` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}